What:		/proc/game_opt/dstate/dump_enable
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write ColorOS 14 GameOpt D-state reporting gate.  Zero disables
		reporting and a nonzero value enables it.  The donor-compatible boot
		default is enabled, but no work occurs until at least one render or
		explicitly interested thread is selected.
Users:		vendor.oplus.hardware.gameopt-service

What:		/proc/game_opt/dstate/duration
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write minimum non-I/O uninterruptible delay, in milliseconds,
		for a selected thread to produce a diagnostic stack report.  The
		OnePlus 9R default is 5 ms.  The donor-compatible range is hardened to
		0 through 60000 ms; values outside that range are rejected.
Users:		vendor.oplus.hardware.gameopt-service

What:		/proc/game_opt/dstate/interested_tids
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write list of up to ten positive decimal thread IDs separated by
		whitespace.  Writing zero clears the list.  The render threads selected
		through `/proc/game_opt/render_thread_info` are tracked in addition to
		this explicit list.

		The 4.14 adaptation uses the existing sched_stat_blocked tracepoint,
		enables scheduler statistics only after userspace selects a thread,
		keeps only one referenced pending task, rate-limits reports to one per
		250 ms, and defers get_wchan and stack walking through irq_work to a
		workqueue.  Its scheduler callback never waits for either reporting
		lock and performs no allocation, stack walk, diagnostic output, or
		workqueue locking.
Users:		vendor.oplus.hardware.gameopt-service
